            <p class="res-row__body">In commercial spaces, glare on computer screens isn't just uncomfortable - it's a measurable productivity problem. OSHA identifies excessive window glare as a workstation environmental hazard that causes eyestrain, headaches, and awkward viewing postures. Glare reduction window film for Philadelphia offices resolves this at the glass - not with blinds that eliminate the views your lease premium paid for.</p>
            <p class="res-row__body">Conference rooms are particularly affected: projector screens and presentation displays become unreadable when afternoon glare enters from south- or west-facing windows. Our commercial-grade glare reduction films for Philadelphia's Center City and University City offices are installed by certified technicians with minimal disruption to daily operations.</p>
